   "survivedEquivalent": [
    {
     "id": "M41",
     "why": "Equivalent on the R7-B.2 bytes: the guard it removes (a clinical handler result outranks the block-choice question, QE-R7B1-01) is now subsumed by the precedence point. In evaluateProgram's decision step a handler returns CLINICAL_HUMAN_REQUIRED only through its own screen (exerciseSubstitution: substitutionClinical; returnAfterPause: interruptionScreen; no other handler or callee returns that status after admission, src/r6-adaptation.mjs and its imports), and clinicalRoute(kind,review) calls the same function on the same review (the factual re-plan context spreads ctx and keeps its review). So handled.status==='CLINICAL_HUMAN_REQUIRED' implies clinical!==null, and then decision0 is clinical before the mutated fragment is read. QE-R7B1-01's behaviour stays covered by the R7-B.1 tests (passing on these bytes) and by neighbor E (scripts/neighbors-r7b2.mjs). The fragment is left in place (smallest diff; no runtime change in U3)."
    }
   ],
